    "issue_alignment": "Matches the described bug: recovery for a broken (size-0) file entry uses rootDir->get(path) (KArchiveDirectory::entry, which descends into subdirectories) but removal uses rootDir->remove(entry) (removeEntry, which only erases direct children). When the located entry lives in a subdirectory, removeEntry no-ops and 'delete entry' leaves a dangling pointer, so deleting the actual containing directory later deletes it again (double delete)."
